    "Id": "vehiclechassisdef_gerrida_GDR-E",
    "Name": "Gerrida",
    "Details": "The E configuration of the Gerrida hovertank mounts two Rotary AC/2s and six Micro Pulse Lasers in its turret, with an AP Gauss Rifle Battery in the front. This combination lets it rush to a crippled target and finish it off, while a Watchdog CEWS protects it with ECM. Its flotation hull keeps it fighting on water even when its propulsion systems are damaged, and an XXL engine gives it exceptional speed for a vehicle of its size.\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Biome Restrictions: None.</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Movement: 7/11 hexes / 210/330 meters.</color></b>\n\n<color=#ffcc00><b>Armor:</b> Ferro-Lamellor (C)\n<b>Structure:</b> Structure\n<b>Values       A        S  </b>\n<b>Front</b>       225     70\n<b>Left</b>         180     70\n<b>Right</b>       180     70\n<b>Rear</b>        150     70\n<b>Turret</b>      200     70\n\n<b>Total</b>      935    350</color>\n\n<color=#ff0000>Quirk: Distracting</color>\n\n<color=#ffcc00> Omni Vehicle</color>",
    "Icon": "Gerrida"
  },
  "YangsThoughts": "This one’s built to chase down anything that’s already hurting and make sure it stays down. Those twin Rotary AC/2s can keep hammering away on the approach, then the AP Gauss Rifles and Micro Pulse Lasers take over once it gets close. For something this big, the Gerrida makes one hell of a pursuit vehicle.",
